<ol class="incident-summary-loop" role="list" aria-label="How knowledge and work stay connected through the Lab">
<li><span class="loop-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><strong>State the need</strong><p>Intent names the export problem; Intent Resolution selects the response and assessment criterion.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="loop-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><strong>Organize the effort</strong><p>Product owns the promised outcome. Project, Goal and Work organize the particular repair.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="loop-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><strong>Prepare the agent</strong><p>Assignment, views, policies and delegation give one temporary session its job, information and limits.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="loop-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div><strong>Preserve the result</strong><p>The observation and evidence support a scoped assessment. Reflections and lessons retain their uncertainty.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="loop-number" aria-hidden="true">05</span><div><strong>Review the requested change</strong><p>The responsible owner decides on exact versions and effects. Each accepted change follows its own route.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="loop-number" aria-hidden="true">06</span><div><strong>Prepare the next session</strong><p>Saved Project State and newly checked views carry knowledge into later work.</p></div></li>
</ol>
